\ Slice 13 phase 3 (R-B8): the mutable write witness. `setat` borrows its
\ array local mutably, takes a mutable reference to one element, and stores
\ through it -- all still generic, monomorphized at `i64` by this call. The
\ borrow is dead once `!` consumes the element reference, so the array can be
\ named and returned afterwards.
: setat ( ['T: Copy 4] 'T -- ['T 4] ) | a v | &!a 2 &!> v ! a ;
: main ( -- )
  0 4 fill | a |
  &!a 0 &!> 10 !  &!a 1 &!> 20 !  &!a 2 &!> 30 !  &!a 3 &!> 40 !
  a 99 setat | b |
  &b 2 &> @ .
  &b 1 &> @ .
  b drop ;
